-- Hard-coded EN + TR translations for all 610 questions.
--
-- Produced by Claude (Anthropic) over 5 parallel sub-agent runs (one per
-- theme), each producing dollar-quoted INSERT VALUES rows. Aggregated into
-- this single migration for repo reproducibility — the prod DB can be
-- rebuilt from these statements with no external API at runtime.
--
-- Per-theme volume:
--   Theme 1 (Principes et valeurs)     : 116 questions × 2 langs = 232 rows
--   Theme 2 (Système institutionnel)   : 119 questions × 2 langs = 238 rows
--   Theme 3 (Droits et devoirs)        : 121 questions × 2 langs = 242 rows
--   Theme 4 (Histoire, géo, culture)   : 146 questions × 2 langs = 292 rows
--   Theme 5 (Vivre en société)         : 108 questions × 2 langs = 216 rows
--   Total                              : 610 questions × 2 langs = 1220 rows
--
-- Translation conventions (consistent across themes):
--   - Faithful, no paraphrase, same length and register as the FR source.
--   - Choice IDs a/b/c/d preserved in original order.
--   - French institutional names (Sécurité sociale, CAF, SMIC, JDC, CIR,
--     Assemblée nationale, Sénat, Conseil constitutionnel, France Travail,
--     CDI/CDD, mairie, préfecture, carte Vitale, etc.) kept in original
--     form with English/Turkish gloss in parentheses on first mention.
--   - Proper nouns (Marianne, Voltaire, Charles de Gaulle, Jeanne d'Arc,
--     Victor Schœlcher, Marseillaise, Mont-Saint-Michel, etc.) kept as-is.
--   - Dates kept numeric (1789, 1944, 14 juillet → 14 July / 14 Temmuz).
--   - Concept terms translated (laïcité → secularism / laiklik,
--     Révolution française → French Revolution / Fransız Devrimi,
--     présomption d'innocence → presumption of innocence / masumiyet karinesi,
--     etc.).
--
-- Idempotent: ON CONFLICT (question_id, lang) DO NOTHING — re-running this
-- file is safe and never overwrites an existing row.

